post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'

==> voice-to-text post-install reminders

    Wayland typing on KDE Plasma (KWin) or GNOME (Mutter) needs the
    ydotoold system service — those compositors don't expose the
    virtual-keyboard-v1 protocol that wtype uses. Enable it now:

        sudo systemctl enable --now ydotoold

    If you're on a wlroots- or smithay-based compositor (Sway, Hyprland,
    niri, river...), wtype handles typing directly and ydotoold is
    unnecessary.

    evdev hotkey capture requires your user to be in the 'input' group.
    Add yourself:

        sudo usermod -aG input $USER

    Log out and back in for the group change to take effect.

    On first launch, open Settings from the tray icon to download a
    whisper model (Base ~82 MB / Small ~180 MB / Medium ~460 MB).

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    post_install
}
